; ANIMATESPRITE: plays a sprite-sheet's frames in place over real time --
; the turtle doesn't move, it just visibly cycles through its grid, each
; frame paced and redrawn rather than snapping straight to the last one.
; Like LOADSPRITE/LOADSPRITESHEET, needs a real window (a GTK-side
; callback -- see load_named_sprite_image in ui.c), so this example only
; makes sense run from the actual app, not the headless test driver.

LOADSPRITESHEET "walker "walker.png 4 2   ; the same 8-frame walk cycle
                                          ; used in spritesheet.logo

SETSPRITE "walker   ; starts on frame 0

ANIMATESPRITE 0.15 24   ; advance one frame every 0.15s, 24 times over --
                        ; three full loops through the 8-frame grid, in
                        ; place, redrawing between each frame

SETSPRITE "NONE   ; back to the default triangle
